 "notes": "Spread layout: left page (102) carries the running head \"HOW TO TRADE IN STOCKS\" and the two printed annotation paragraphs, vertically aligned with the ledger rows they describe; right page (103) carries the ledger grid headed \"CHART ONE\" with the Livermore Market Key crest at top right. Grid group labels printed mid-header row: \"U. S. STEEL\", \"BETHLEHEM STEEL\", \"KEY PRICE\"; 18 vertical column headers as specified. Dated rows run MAR23 1938 through MAY 4 1938 (trading days Mon-Sat; APR.1, APR 4-8, 11-12, 18-27, SAT.30, MAY 3-4 have no entries and are omitted per instructions). Every row where US, BS and KP all have entries passes the checksum KP = US + BS; checksums were also used to fix ambiguous fraction glyphs (noted per cell). Recurring quirk: a small comma-like tick sometimes follows whole numbers (BS 43 on Mar 29, KP 97 on Apr 13, US 43 on Apr 28); where checksum-testable it always resolves to a whole number, so it is treated as a stray mark, not a fraction numerator. Drawn pivotal underlines observed: heavy single black bars (header 65 3/4, 48 1/2, 62 1/8, 91 3/4; Mar 31 row 38/40/78; Apr 16 row 49/52/101), heavy single red lines (header 57, 65 7/8, 122 3/4, 128), and clearly double red lines (header 43 1/4 and 50 1/8). All row/ink assignments cross-checked against the color convention (UT black, DT red, others blue) with no contradictions.",
